Z||000000||aubicon||12-25-2000||04:38 PM||||I just finnished breaking my fiero bown to the frame and now i want to make it into a targa top(where the roof section above the above the driver and the passanger is removed but the windseild and the rear window remain) like they do on the vetts and those dam Honda del sols. well on to the question i know i have to reinforce the frame to maintain rigitity, i could just use one of the reinforcement frames from a convertable kit by why waste the money if there is an easy way to weld in some suports. any advise would be apriciated and all oppinions will be enjoyed. thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||PAUL88GT||12-25-2000||08:07 PM||||I don't have an answer for you. Just wanted to say welcome to the forum.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||12-25-2000||08:27 PM||||I've never did one either. But I have seen one done. The guy used square stock tubing, using the front to back piecies as the coolent pipes. Then an X of tubing in the center for support. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||12-25-2000||09:46 PM||||i think pisa sells an x frame but i think it's the kind where you can't get your gas tank out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||12-25-2000||10:30 PM||||Bob at Twin Lakes Fiero does convertable conversions. He Drives Square stock steel thru the frame rails and welds them to the front and rear sub-frames. A friend is doing this to his 84 also. The car does not flex.<BR>It is better than the "X" frame since you cannot see it, it does not interfere with anything, and it is strong enough that that we were able to put the 84 on a dolly under the center of the car to move it around the garage. (Had to do it to paint his 87 GT)<BR>You can call Bob and ask him anything else about the process at 217-379-9140.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-25-2000).]||||reg||1
